<description>
Overlay the four monochrome quadrant masks onto their common half-size canvas.

Input structure
The input is a 2x2 arrangement of equal-size regions on a uniform background.
Each region contains foreground pixels of exactly one color, forming one mask
at the output scale.

Rule
Start with a background output the size of one region. Stamp the masks from
back to front by quadrant position: top-left, bottom-right, bottom-left,
then top-right. Later masks overwrite earlier masks where they overlap.

Key insight
Folding all four quadrants onto the same coordinates gives the output
canvas; the quadrant positions encode the visible layer stack.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_in_order",
  "src": "monochrome foreground masks s in the 2x2 quadrants, ordered back-to-front by quadrant position: top-left, bottom-right, bottom-left, top-right",
  "dst": "layers d of the half-size output canvas ordered back-to-front",
  "match_cond": "rank(s) == rank(d)",
  "transform": "fold each mask onto its local coordinates and stamp it with its quadrant color; later layers overwrite earlier overlaps",
  "grid_shape": "output is one quadrant: input height/2 by input width/2"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 2N x 2M where N=4, M=4 [observed]; solver requires even dims
  background: 0
  quadrants: 4 equal NxM regions (TL, TR, BL, BR), each with exactly 1 distinct fg color
  colors: TL=4, TR=5, BL=6, BR=9 [observed]; solver only requires 4 distinct non-bg colors
  fg_density: 25-75% per quadrant (4-12 of 16 pixels when N=M=4)
  connectivity: 1-4 connected components per mask; no constraint on shape
  union_coverage: 81-100% of output cells covered by at least 1 mask; 0-3 bg cells in output
  stacking_order: TL(back) -> BR -> BL -> TR(front); later layers overwrite earlier
  output: NxM canvas; stamp masks back-to-front, each mask painted in its quadrant color

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size N, M (use 4x4 for now; could generalize to 3-6)
    2. Choose 4 distinct non-bg colors for TL, TR, BL, BR
    3. Build the NxM output canvas by generating 4 random binary masks (one per quadrant)
       with fg density 25-75% each and union coverage >= 80%
    4. Assign stacking order TL(back), BR, BL, TR(front) and paint the output
    5. Derive input by placing each mask in its quadrant position within a 2Nx2M grid,
       coloring fg pixels with that quadrant's color, bg elsewhere
  notes: >
    Output-first guarantees valid overlap and stacking. Generate masks independently,
    then verify union coverage >= 80%; regenerate if too sparse.
```
